{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>And this is what their father spoke to them, and he blessed them.</b> But are there not some among them whom he did not bless but rather rebuked? Rather, this is its meaning: 'And this is what their father spoke to them' — that which is stated in the matter. One might say he did not bless Reuben, Simeon, and Levi — therefore Scripture says ״וַיְבָרֶךְ אוֹתָם״ — all of them are included." "<b>Each according to his blessing.</b> The blessing destined to come upon each and every one." "<b>He blessed them.</b> It should have said only ״אִישׁ אֲשֶׁר כְּבִרְכָתוֹ בֵּרַךְ אוֹתוֹ״ — what does Scripture teach by saying ״בֵּרַךְ אוֹתָם״? Because He gave Judah the might of a lion, and Benjamin the snatching of a wolf, and Naphtali the swiftness of a deer — one might say he did not include them all in all the blessings; Scripture teaches by saying ״בֵּרַךְ אוֹתָם״."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:04:20.576373886Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}